# `thm:torsion-free` and `cor:regular-nonmf-algebra` forms over the five open residuals

Lane gl-assembly-09.  `non_mf_groups_exist.tex`:

* census line 297 (284 in older numberings), `\label{thm:torsion-free}`:
  > There is a two-generated, finitely presented, torsion-free, acylindrically hyperbolic group $Q$
  > with property (T) such that every homomorphism from $Q$ to an MF group is trivial.  In
  > particular, no nontrivial quotient of $Q$ is MF.
* census line 2204 (1718–1722 in older numberings), `\label{cor:regular-nonmf-algebra}`:
  > The algebra $C^*_{\mathrm r}(Q)$ is separable, unital, simple, and generated by two unitaries.
  > It has a unique tracial state and stable rank one, and it is stably finite but not MF.

Each theorem applies the matching `TorsionFreeGreendlingerForms.*_of_greendlinger`
(`TorsionFreeGreendlingerForms.lean:160-222`) to `leastAreaLeaf_of_openResidualsBelow`.  The
remaining hypothesis `hopen` is explained in `GreendlingerClosedForms/Leaf`.
-/

